--- ORIGINAL approach (WRONG - uses 'channel_name' column that doesn't exist)
+++ FIXED approach (uses 'platform' and 'token' columns that actually exist)

The channels table schema is:
- id (UUID)
- user_id (UUID FK)
- platform (VARCHAR) — 'telegram', 'discord', 'slack', 'signal'
- token (VARCHAR) — the bot/app token
- (possibly verified, created_at, etc.)

CHANGE ALL supabase.table('channels').upsert({...}) calls to use:
{
  'user_id': user_id,
  'platform': channel_name,  # 'telegram', 'discord', etc.
  'token': bot_token,        # the actual token
  ...other fields...
}

INSTEAD OF:
{
  'user_id': user_id,
  'channel_name': 'telegram',  # WRONG - column doesn't exist
  'config': {...},             # WRONG - column doesn't exist
  ...
}
